all Street on Tuesday after markets close. Here's a chart for what some are calling The Trillion Club: Guggenheim Partners analyst Robert Cihra–who expects solid iPhone sales (43 million units, up 4% year-over-year) and strong Services performance ($9.3 billion, up 28% year-over-year)–raised his quarterly revenue estimate to $52.9 billion from $52.4 billion. Reblog What to Read Next", "external_links": ["https://www.tumblr.com/widgets/share/tool?posttype=link&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.barrons.com%2Farticles%2Fapple-earnings-expect-strong-q3-services-revenue-1532958805%3Fmod%3Dyahoobarrons%26ru%3Dyahoo%26yptr%3Dyahoo%26soc_src%3Dsocial-sh%26soc_trk%3Dtu&content=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.barrons.com%2Farticles%2Fapple-earnings-expect-strong-q3-services-revenue-1532958805%3Fmod%3Dyahoobarrons%26ru%3Dyahoo%26yptr%3Dyahoo%26soc_src%3Dsocial-sh%26soc_trk%3Dtu&caption=The%20race%20to%20the%20mythical%20%241%20trillion%20mark"], "published": "2018-07-30T17:49:00.000+03:00", "crawled": "2018-07-31T00:06:09.000+03:00", "highlightTitle": ""}